Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=3: as =2, and guest writes made while a guard is up reach the caches only after its fence; off by default

T89, batch t89-a (door walk): =2 kept the speed (17.1 fps against 17.9) and the cut to Link's
house was clean in 3 of 3 runs, but one or two small dark glitches stayed (50-100 ms in all
against 517 for the control), the fade was out of order in 2 of 3, and with
EDEN_UP_AHEAD_ALWAYS it had nine moments at 20.3 fps. The waiting guard had none of these.

With =2 a write made after the present was still gathered and applied while the frame in flight
drew. For most pages that only marks them for an upload, which then reads the copy. But a write
into memory the GPU owns is uploaded into the host buffer at once (the buffer cache's inline
page writes), and a texture the write touches is uploaded again from memory.

=3: GPU::GatherAndApply gathers nothing while a guard is up, so what the cores collect then stays
with them (still in ForEachPendingCpuWrite's view) until the first gather after the guard is
lifted. The writes made before the present are the frame's own: nx2:vi2 PresentClientBuffer
gathers them just before the guard goes up (GPU::GatherForAheadGuard, on its own thread; one
mutex keeps the two gathers apart) and the GPU thread's next gather applies them.

---
diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
index 1781f32..f29b66e 100644
--- a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
+++ b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
@@ -2005,6 +2005,12 @@ private:
             const bool previous_reached =
                 m_previous_fence_id < 192 &&
                 syncpoints.IsReadyGuest(m_previous_fence_id, m_previous_fence_value);
+            // =3: what the cores collected up to here was written before this present, so it is
+            // this frame's own: gathered now, applied by the GPU thread's next gather. What they
+            // collect while the guard is up waits for its fence.
+            if (VideoCommon::AheadGuard::Mode() == 3 && !syncpoints.IsReadyGuest(~w[22], w[24])) {
+                system.GPU().GatherForAheadGuard();
+            }
             VideoCommon::AheadGuard::AtPresent(m_presents, ~w[22], w[24], previous_reached,
                                                syncpoints, system.Host1x().MemoryManager());
         }
